    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273-a3">

                <pb facs="0500" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    40.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stuart to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Her Britannic Majesty</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 14,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I am authorized by the
                    diplomatic corps of this city, of which I have the honor to be the dean, to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of this date, addressed to Mr. Langston,
                    minister resident of the United States, in which you request him to communicate
                    with his colleagues to take measures dictated by the circumstances having in
                    view the interests of humanity.</p>
                <p>The corps diplomatique, having taken into consideration this letter, unanimously
                    agrees that under the circumstances the initiative does not belong to them; but
                    they are ready to take into consideration all propositions coming from the
                    government in <pb facs="0501" n="439" xml:id="pg439"/> the interests of
                    humanity, and having in view to avoid the dangers which seem to menace the
                    persons and property of those who reside in Port au Prince.</p>
                <p>Please accept, Mr. Secretary of State, the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>R. STUART.</item>
                            <item>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Felix Carrié</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of Foreign Affairs, Port
                                    au Prince.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—I herewith inclose a copy of the communication received this morning
                        from General Tanis.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
